e title of a collapsible section is the visible header shown at the top of the section. A collapsible section is a standard section with an added option that allows it to expand or collapse on demand. This is empty in most cases. Only used when section is collapsible.",collapsible_settings:"Settings that control whether the section is rendered as a collapsible (accordion) section and how it looks. All fields are stored independently of each other so values are preserved when toggles are flipped.",collapsible_settings_is_collapsible:"Whether the section is rendered as a collapsible (accordion) section. This is the sole control for collapsibility; set true to make the section collapsible and false to make it regular. Toggling this does not modify any other field in this group.",collapsible_settings_title:"The header text of the collapsible section. Only rendered when both `isCollapsible` and `isTitleEnabled` are true, but stored independently so the value survives toggling either of them off.",collapsible_settings_is_title_enabled:"Whether the section title is displayed at the top of the collapsible section. Only effective when `isCollapsible` is true.",collapsible_settings_title_heading_level:"Heading level used to render the section title (H2, H3, or H4). Only effective when both `isCollapsible` and `isTitleEnabled` are true.",collapsible_settings_is_expanded_by_default:"Default display state of the collapsible section when the page is first loaded. true means expanded, false means collapsed. Only effective when `isCollapsible` is true.",collapsible_settings_icon_alignment:'Alignment of the expand/collapse icon on a collapsible section. "left" places the icon before the title, "right" places it after. Only effective when `isCollapsible` is true.',collapsible_settings_show_divider_line:"Whether a divider line is shown between this collapsible section and the next. Only effective when `isCollapsible` is true.",section_layout:"Section layout defines how columns are arranged within a section. The layout determines the number of columns, their relative widths, and how web parts can be placed. When adding a section in Edit mode, you choose a layout to control how content will be organized.",section_alignment:"Section alignment is how content inside multiple columns is vertically aligned. This setting controls whether web parts in different columns start at the same top position, are centered, or aligned to the bottom of the section.",section_emphasis:"Section emphasis controls the visual background style of a section. It helps distinguish one section from another, highlight important content, or provide visual rhythm on a page. Emphasis is applied at the section level and affects all its columns and web parts.",section_background:"Section background defines the visual treatment behind all columns and controls. It can include images, overlays, or other styling that ensures foreground content remains readable.",section_background_overlay:"The overlay applied to a section background is a translucent color or gradient that sits above the background image. Use it to improve contrast for text and web parts. Provide color and opacity when needed.",section_background_use_light_text:"Set this to true when the background requires light-colored foreground text to maintain readability. Keep it false when standard or dark text provides sufficient contrast.",control_flexible_layout_position:"Flexible layout positioning allows controls to be placed precisely on a grid. Provide integer x and y coordinates (measured in grid columns and rows) along with width and height in grid units. Use this only when the section layout is flexible. Flexible sections contain a grid that has 70 columns total.",control_flexible_layout_position_x:"Horizontal grid start position for a control inside a flexible section.",control_flexible_layout_position_y:"Vertical grid start position for a control inside a flexible section.",control_flexible_layout_position_width:"Number of grid columns spanned by the control inside a flexible section.",control_flexible_layout_position_height:"Number of grid rows spanned by the control inside a flexible section. The client may expand or shrink this after render; capture the final value and shift downstream controls only as needed so no unexpected overlaps are added.",canvas:"The canvas is the main surface of a modern SharePoint page. Regular layouts are horizontal sections with columns for main content. A vertical layout is an optional side column for supporting web parts.",instance_id:"A unique identifier for a specific instance on the page. It must be globally unique within the page and remain stable once assigned — it should never change for the same instance across updates."},page:{page_description:"Page description for preview surfaces such as search results, SharePoint news, and highlighted content. Leave empty unless the existing description is AI-generated or the user is asking to update it. If empty, SharePoint will auto-generate the description from the page content. This value is not rendered on the page canvas; users only see it by opening the page details pane.",page_thumbnail:"Page thumbnail for preview surfaces such as search results, SharePoint news, and highlighted content. Leave empty unless the user is asking to update it. If empty, SharePoint will auto-generate the thumbnail from the page title area or the first web part. This value is not rendered on the page canvas; users only see it by opening the page details pane.",page:"A page is a list item in the Site Pages library with metadata fields and canvas content."}};class Q extends C.BaseAIObject{get classUniqueId(){return Q.classUniqueId}getDefaultSystemPrompt(){return P.canvas.control_flexible_layout_position}initDefaultMetadata(){return{dataUsage:C.VIBE_AUTHORING_ONLY_DATA_USAGE}}initStructure(){return{x:new C.AIInteger({customPrompts:{systemPromptForAI:P.canvas.control_flexible_layout_position_x},customMetadata:{dataUsage: